# Build-time environment. `VITE_COVALENT_KEY` — the GoldRush key that reads BNB
# history, since that chain's explorer data is sold rather than served — lives in
# `.env.local`, which Vite loads for every mode and git never sees. The last key
# was committed once and had to be rotated at the provider; this is what stops the
# next one going the same way. `.env.example` is the committed half: names, no values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Release signing material. Never commit these: the keystore and its passwords are
# what prove an update came from you, and losing control of them is unrecoverable.
src-tauri/gen/android/keystore.properties
src-tauri/gen/android/*.jks
src-tauri/gen/android/*.keystore
